Z||000000||Gokart||06-29-2000||07:26 AM||||Now I know why I couldn't find my 180 thermo from last summer...I must have thrown it out because for some reason my GT runs AND seems to start better with the 195 thermo installed! Anyone else experience this? ||||reg||4
Z||000001||WisconsinGT||06-29-2000||08:50 AM||||Gokart,<P>I have the exact opposite situation. Last weekend I put a 180 stat in my 88GT 2.8 auto. I have more power. It feels real goood. She pulls hard. Where as before it was doggy taking off from a dead start. ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||06-29-2000||02:32 PM||||I have been running a 180 stat since I got it smogged last september (V6).  It seems to run great (the rebuild might have something to do with that), but my gas mileage sucks.  I only get around 18 around town.  I was wondering if a cooler coolant temperature would make it get lower gas mileage?<P>||||reg||3
